<title>UK: Saxon Assets Secs sets $467 mln 14-tranche bond.</title>
<headline>Saxon Assets Secs sets $467 mln 14-tranche bond.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saxon Asset Securities Trust 1997-2 has launched a 14-tranche home equity loan asset-backed bond for a total of $467 million, lead manager Merrill Lynch said.</p>
<p>The largest tranche, of class AV-1 notes, total $294 million. With a June 2027 legal maturity, these notes have an expected average life of 2.14 years.</p>
<p>They will be priced to yield around 21 basis points over one-month Libor and are rated triple-A by Moody's and Fitch.</p>
<p>The remaining 13 tranches range in size between $31 million and $2.0 million.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
</text>
